# Smart-Serve — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Docker Compose reads this file and injects the variables into the container; the app
# itself never parses `.env` (ADR-009). Every variable here is optional — the values shown
# are the defaults the container uses when they are unset.
#
# Only *operational* settings live in the environment. Every interpretation threshold
# (temperature limits, sector thresholds, retention, squelch windows) is configured in the
# web UI and stored in SQLite, deliberately: a threshold you must restart the container to
# change is a threshold nobody tunes.

# HTTP listen address. If you change the port, change the compose `ports:` mapping too.
SMARTSERVE_ADDR=:8080

# SQLite database path. Leave this alone unless you mount the data volume elsewhere.
SMARTSERVE_DB=/data/smartserve.db

# URL subpath, for hosting behind a proxy at e.g. https://host/smartserve/ (ADR-015).
# Leave unset (or "/") when the app is served from the root.
#SMARTSERVE_BASE_PATH=/smartserve

# Per-command timeout for smartctl and lsblk, in seconds.
#SMARTSERVE_COMMAND_TIMEOUT=15

# What to do when a scheduled scan was missed while the container was down:
# `skip` waits for the next scheduled fire, `run_once` runs it at startup.
#SMARTSERVE_MISSED_RUN_POLICY=skip

# debug | info | warn | error
#SMARTSERVE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Timezone used for cron-style schedules and for displayed timestamps.
TZ=Etc/UTC

# --- Notification channel overrides ---------------------------------------------------
#
# A channel's fields can be supplied here instead of through the web UI, which is how you keep
# a token out of the /data volume and therefore out of its backups. Variables are named after
# the channel's LABEL — uppercased, with each run of punctuation reduced to an underscore — and
# the channel editor prints the exact prefix for each channel, so the name never has to be
# guessed.
#
#   SMARTSERVE_CHANNEL_<LABEL>_<FIELD>          the value
#   SMARTSERVE_CHANNEL_<LABEL>_<FIELD>_FILE     a file to read the value from
#
# Examples. Every string field works, not only the secret ones, and precedence is
# environment > file > database:
#
#   A channel labelled "Critical alerts", its token field:
#SMARTSERVE_CHANNEL_CRITICAL_ALERTS_TOKEN=tk_abc123
#
#   The same channel, reading the token from a mounted file so it never appears here:
#SMARTSERVE_CHANNEL_CRITICAL_ALERTS_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token
#
#   Pointing a channel at a different server per environment:
#SMARTSERVE_CHANNEL_WEEKLY_DIGEST_SERVER=https://ntfy.internal
#
# A _FILE variable that points at a missing or empty file is an error, not a fallback: the
# send fails and the delivery log says why, rather than quietly using a stale token. Renaming
# a channel changes its variable names — the editor badges each field the deployment supplies,
# so the mismatch is visible. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §Secrets and ADR-022.
